      "id": "wiring-1",
      "reason": "the missing edge is exactly the one the same revision added for s81, and without it s13's CPU arm is dispatched against a known-red population.",
      "text": "s83 removes the station's dominant remaining CPU cost (`resumption.sweep` at 88 % of one thread, `_lifted_holds` 30 % of it in the cited 1,308-sample profile), yet plan-section-depends-on gives s13 only s81, so the DAG would admit s13 \u2014 whose done-when measures \"the station alone \u2026 uses under 5 % of one core\" over 60 s with at least 30 live runs \u2014 before the cost s83 removes has been removed, and that arm cannot pass until s83 lands",
      "type": "wiring",
      "would_change": true
    },
    {
      "anchor": "/home/ITER/mcintos/.config/reckon/crew/reports/reckon/plan-review/the-monitor-reads-each-fact-once/r-20261117T045922382985-plan-review-of-the-monitor-reads-each-fact-once/plan.html:816",
      "id": "reasoning-1",
      "reason": "the reuse directive is a guess the node must test against `file_memo` and will fail, costing a round, and the reuse map belongs to the node brief, not to plan text.",
      "text": "the Deliverable fixes the mechanism, not only the endpoint: \"The set and the byte offset it has read up to are held against the log's file identity\" plus \"Use `reckon/file_memo.py` rather than a private cache\" specify the cache's shape and the module to extend, and the two are incompatible as written because `file_memo.memoized`/`memoized_key` hand back a whole stored value from a `compute()` that takes no arguments (reckon/file_memo.py:362-445), so neither can extend an offset and the node would have to keep private state anyway",
      "type": "reasoning",
      "would_change": true
    }
  ],
