    "anchors_resolve": "pass \u2014 `reckon/crew/resumption.py` near line 780 is `_lifted_holds`, `reckon/file_memo.py` exists, the recovery log resolves at 41,993,522 bytes, and the plan-section-depends-on entry it gains (`s13`) resolves.",
    "done_when": "pass \u2014 s83's four cases are all executed measurements and the declared control (\"at the base revision the second call decodes 5,000 lines\") is true at base, since `_lifted_holds` re-reads and decodes the whole log on every call (reckon/crew/resumption.py:780-804); case (a)'s reference is the fixture's own expected pairs, which the test can compute because it writes the log.",
